glossary:
  - term: Ogdoad
    gloss: The eight deities, Nun among them, representing ancient Egyptian
      primordial Chaos; none of them had temples or any center of worship.
    from: Nun is one of the eight deities of the [[ Ogdoad | ogdoad-egyptian ]]
      representing [[ ancient Egyptian primordial Chaos |
      isfet-egyptian-mythology ]] from which the [[ primordial mound | benben
      ]] arose. ... Like the other Ogdoad deities, Nu did not have temples or
      any center of worship.
  - term: Benben
    gloss: A pyramid mound, which emerged amid the primal chaos of the primordial
      waters.
    from: The universe was enrapt by a vast mass of primordial waters, and the
      Benben, a pyramid mound, emerged amid this primal chaos.
  - term: Naunet
    gloss: "Nun's consort, or his female aspect: the name //Nu// with a female
      gender ending, represented as a snake or snake-headed woman."
