      or !!Naunet!! ... Naunet (also spelt Nunet) is the female aspect, which
      is the name //Nu// with a female gender ending. ... Naunet is
      represented as a snake or snake-headed woman.
  - term: Solar barque
    gloss: The boat Nun is typically shown holding aloft, carrying the new-born
      sun out of the waters of creation.
    from: he was typically depicted in ancient Egyptian art holding aloft the [[
      solar barque ]] or the sun disc. ... Nun lifts the [[ solar barque ]]
      with the new-born sun from the waters of creation.
  - term: Mehet-Weret
    gloss: A figure portrayed as a cow with a sun disk between her horns who, in
